<section class="article-content">

    <div class="section-header">

        <span class="section-kicker">

            SAFETY

        </span>

        <h2>

            Is Cali Safe?

        </h2>

    </div>

    <p>
        We debated whether this should appear at the beginning of the guide.
    </p>
    <p>
    As locals, safety isn't something that dominates our everyday conversations. We go to work, meet friends, enjoy restaurants, dance salsa, hike in the mountains, and live our lives much like people do in any other large city.
    </p>
    <p>
    But as local tour guides, we know that for many international travelers, this is the first question they have. In fact, it is often the reason they hesitate to visit Cali at all.
    </p>
    <p>
    So rather than asking you to wait until the end of the guide, we'd rather address it right away.
    </p>
    <p>
    The short answer is yes: thousands of travelers visit Cali every year and have an incredible experience. The longer answer is that, like most major cities in Latin America—and many large cities around the world—your experience depends on knowing where to go, how to get around, and using a bit of common sense.
    </p>
    <p>
    There are neighborhoods we'd recommend avoiding, just as there are neighborhoods we happily recommend to our own friends and family. There are times when taking an Uber is the smarter choice than walking, and there are areas where you'll find locals, families, cafés, parks, and people simply enjoying their day.
    </p>
    <p>
    If you've only seen Cali through headlines or social media, it's understandable that you might have a very different picture in your mind. Headlines tend to focus on exceptional events, not on the millions of ordinary moments that make up daily life in a city of more than two million people.
    </p>
    <p>
    Our goal isn't to convince you that Cali is perfect. It isn't. No large city is.
    </p>
    <p>
    Our goal is to give you honest, practical advice so you can experience the city the way we do: with awareness, confidence, and an open mind.
    </p>
    <p>
    Now that we've addressed the 'elephant in the room', let's get to the fun part: discovering why so many visitors leave Cali wondering why they didn't come sooner.
    </p>

</section>

<div class="experience-bubble">

    <span class="experience-bubble__label">

        AFTER HUNDREDS OF TOURS

    </span>

    <p>

        The vast majority of our guests arrive in Cali with the same concern:
        safety.

    </p>

    <p>

        Ironically, it's also the topic they talk about the least by the end of
        their trip.

    </p>

    <p>

        Instead, they remember the salsa, the breezy afternoons, the people they met, the
        food, and the feeling of discovering a city that turned out to be very
        different from what they expected.

    </p>

    <span class="experience-bubble__author">

        — Juan Camilo<br>

        Founder, Cali Cultural Tours

    </span>

</div>

